WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.688
Qian Liu, a wise man in his fifties, founded the kingdom of Wuyue at Hangzhou.

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:12.038
While war raged everywhere in the Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms, only Wuyue kept a rare peace.

00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:16.996
The people farmed in peace, undisturbed by the fires of war.

00:00:17.346 --> 00:00:24.210
Qian Liu ordered great waterworks; the craftsmen built dikes, and clear water flowed into the fields.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.424
The rivers no longer flooded, and the farmland was well irrigated.

00:00:28.774 --> 00:00:35.206
The rice harvest was rich, the markets lively and prosperous, and merchant ships came and went.

00:00:35.556 --> 00:00:39.948
People's lives grew ever more prosperous and peaceful.

00:00:40.298 --> 00:00:46.130
The common people lived and worked in contentment, all grateful to this king who cherished his people.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.952
Later generations used the four words 'protect the borders, bring peace to the people' to describe Wuyue's policy.

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:57.774
This peace was the most precious gift in an age of chaos.

